            // Pattern: q <= {q[1] ^ q[2], q[0], q[2]} when L=0.
            // When L=1: load r_in.
            // We map r_in to the MSB and shift, using q_in for the LSB or as control.
            // To be deterministic and synthesizable with the given ports:
            q_reg <= {q_in, q_reg[2:1]}; 
            // This shifts q_reg[2:1] right by one, inserts q_in at LSB, and MSB becomes q_reg[2] (shifted out).
            // Adjustment to match full_module shift: q_reg <= {q_reg[2], q_in, q_reg[1]}; 
            // Let's re-evaluate based on typical shift register behavior and the provided ports.
        end else begin
            // Shift mode: emulate full_module shift pattern
            // full_module: q <= {q[1] ^ q[2], q[0], q[2]}
